From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:34:05 -0647
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: net: nfc: nxp,nci: Add the ST ST54L

The ST54L in the Google Pixel 9a speaks plain NCI over I2C with an
enable line and an interrupt, the transport the nxp-nci driver
implements, rather than the NDLC framing of ST's ST21NFCB family
(st,st21nfcb-i2c), whose initialisation timed out on it. Add it as a
compatible with nxp,nxp-nci-i2c as the fallback.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/nfc/nxp,nci.yaml | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/nfc/nxp,nci.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/nfc/nxp,nci.yaml
index 4f3847f64..fbf2b14f6 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/nfc/nxp,nci.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/nfc/nxp,nci.yaml
@@ -6,6 +6,10 @@ $schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
 
 title: NXP Semiconductors NCI NFC controller
 
+description:
+  NFC controllers that speak plain NCI over I2C, with an enable line and an
+  interrupt. Besides NXP's, ST's ST54L uses the same transport.
+
 maintainers:
   - Krzysztof Kozlowski <krzk@kernel.org>
 
@@ -19,6 +23,7 @@ properties:
               - nxp,pn547
               - nxp,pn553
               - nxp,pn557
+              - st,st54l
           - const: nxp,nxp-nci-i2c
 
   enable-gpios:
